1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,024
This iron centre has seven neighbours: it is a pentagonal bipyramid.

2
00:00:04,244 --> 00:00:05,851
Here we replay our recorded run.

3
00:00:06,071 --> 00:00:10,285
Gemini answers the same question from CIF text, from three rendered images,

4
00:00:10,285 --> 00:00:13,487
through an interactive viewer, and with MolCrysKit tools.

5
00:00:13,707 --> 00:00:17,409
From the text and the tools it gets seven, pentagonal bipyramid.

6
00:00:17,629 --> 00:00:23,332
From the images and the viewer it says six, octahedral, and so does DeepSeek in the viewer.

7
00:00:23,552 --> 00:00:25,729
That gap is the question behind CrystalSight.

8
00:00:26,379 --> 00:00:29,743
Before a database structure is used for simulation, someone checks it.

9
00:00:29,963 --> 00:00:34,305
Are hydrogens missing? Is it disordered? What is the metal's coordination?

10
00:00:34,305 --> 00:00:36,300
Can it go straight into DFT or MD?

11
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:41,792
LLM agents are increasingly asked to do this
check, and we can give them the structure as text,

12
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:45,954
as images rendered with MatterVis, like these, or as an interactive viewer.

13
00:00:46,174 --> 00:00:47,585
We don't know whether those are equivalent.

14
00:00:48,235 --> 00:00:52,208
CrystalSight asks the same questions about the same structures:

15
00:00:52,208 --> 00:00:58,263
67 molecular crystals from the Crystallography
Open Database and 247 questions in five families:

16
00:00:58,263 --> 00:01:04,003
hydrogens, disorder, metal coordination, usability for simulation, and pairwise comparison.

17
00:01:04,223 --> 00:01:05,688
Each task has a question,

18
00:01:05,688 --> 00:01:10,728
a JSON answer schema and a gold answer
computed with MolCrysKit plus documented rules.

19
00:01:11,378 --> 00:01:15,424
Scoring is automatic, with partial credit: flag the problem correctly,

20
00:01:15,424 --> 00:01:20,221
then name what is affected; coordination splits credit between number and geometry.

21
00:01:20,441 --> 00:01:23,049
The no-problem baseline always answers "clean",

22
00:01:23,049 --> 00:01:26,545
or the most common gold answer for coordination and comparison.

23
00:01:26,765 --> 00:01:29,141
The random baseline guesses with the right answer type.

24
00:01:29,361 --> 00:01:33,522
The balanced score averages problem and clean structures within each family,

25
00:01:33,522 --> 00:01:35,165
then across the five families.

26
00:01:35,815 --> 00:01:41,256
The model sees one channel at a time: CIF text
with give-away disorder annotations stripped;

27
00:01:41,256 --> 00:01:45,100
the unstripped CIF as a leakage control; three MatterVis renders;

28
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:50,186
or the interactive MatterVis viewer shown here, which it can rotate, zoom and relabel.

29
00:01:50,406 --> 00:01:54,630
Tool access to MolCrysKit is reported separately as a reference upper bound,

30
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:57,131
because those tools compute the gold answers.

31
00:01:57,550 --> 00:02:03,169
These structure checks put text ahead of pictures, but most could be answered from one

32
00:02:03,169 --> 00:02:08,984
line of the file. So we added two spatial sets of twenty questions each. Gold answers are

33
00:02:08,984 --> 00:02:14,276
computed from geometry and stay the same when every cutoff moves by five percent.

34
00:02:14,876 --> 00:02:23,631
On the easy set, CIF text alone scores 0.70 to 0.82. On the hard set, which asks for

35
00:02:23,631 --> 00:02:32,908
symmetry copies, hydrogen-bond paths, rings and shell counts, text drops to 0.20 to 0.43.

36
00:02:33,508 --> 00:02:39,891
Rendered images and the ASCII viewer stay near chance, at 0.10 to 0.22, even with a

37
00:02:39,891 --> 00:02:44,275
hydrogen-bond overlay and a distance query in the viewer.

38
00:02:44,875 --> 00:02:51,339
Give the same models six small geometry tools that return raw lists, and both reach about

39
00:02:51,339 --> 00:02:56,278
0.75. Here one call to the ring tool is enough for the right answer.

40
00:02:56,878 --> 00:03:03,093
Per family, only the nearest-partner question is solved without tools. Disorder replicas

41
00:03:03,093 --> 00:03:05,070
stay hard for every channel.

42
00:03:05,670 --> 00:03:11,054
We found that published hydrogen-bond tables leaked answers, removed them, fixed a

43
00:03:11,054 --> 00:03:16,898
stripping bug and re-ran the affected text channels. The sets are small, with two models,

44
00:03:16,898 --> 00:03:20,312
and the tools were written for these question types.

45
00:03:21,135 --> 00:03:21,739
There are limits.

46
00:03:21,959 --> 00:03:24,932
Gold labels depend on heuristic thresholds,

47
00:03:24,932 --> 00:03:30,809
and even with tools disorder reaches only 0.87 to 0.89, so some labels are ambiguous.

48
00:03:31,029 --> 00:03:34,586
We cover 67 structures and two models with one run each,

49
00:03:34,586 --> 00:03:37,762
and the coordination family has only 11 questions.

50
00:03:37,982 --> 00:03:42,508
Next: more structures, models and repeated runs, occupancy-aware renders,

51
00:03:42,508 --> 00:03:46,042
and agents that combine viewing with text or tool checks.

52
00:03:46,692 --> 00:03:49,902
The code, tasks, ground truth and figures are open,

53
00:03:49,902 --> 00:03:52,798
and a mock run like this one needs no API key.

54
00:03:53,018 --> 00:03:54,826
Try your own model, or add a channel.

55
00:03:55,046 --> 00:03:55,887
The link is below.
